  "Description":          "The Environment Description (XRV-END) AIM captures raw Data from the Real and Virtual Environments including audio, visual, and other data in a variety of formats defined by the Qualifier standard; using Script-Venue Associations, identifies and separates the Performance elements, Participant elements and Operator elements that are relevant to subsequent processing; packages them into Performance, Participant, and Operator Descriptors for both the Real and Virtual Environments, and a combination of all Descriptors called Show Descriptors; and passes the Descriptors to downstream AIMs.",

